      $$Eritrea offers unique tourism assets including Asmara's UNESCO-listed Italian art deco architecture, Red Sea coral reefs and diving, Massawa's Ottoman-Italian heritage, ancient Adulis archaeological site, and highland landscapes. Tourism sector is severely underdeveloped due to political isolation, visa restrictions, limited air connectivity, and minimal international awareness. Hospitality infrastructure is basic beyond Asmara. The sector represents very long-term opportunity for heritage tourism, Red Sea diving tourism, architectural tourism, and destination development contingent on political opening, visa liberalization, air connectivity improvement, and destination marketing serving specialized heritage and diving tourism niches as accessibility improves.$$,
      35, 52, 7, 'explorer'),

