      $$Madagascar's digital infrastructure is expanding through submarine cable landings, mobile network growth, fiber backbone development, and digital services addressing island connectivity challenges.$$,
      $$Madagascar benefits from submarine cable landings providing international bandwidth with fiber backbone expansion connecting major cities. Mobile telecommunications are growing with increasing smartphone penetration. Internet access is improving but remains limited in rural areas. E-government services and digital identity programs are developing. Island geography creates connectivity challenges for remote regions. ICT sector serves growing urban population and tourism economy. The sector represents opportunity for mobile broadband expansion, rural connectivity investment, digital public infrastructure, fintech adoption, and technology innovation supporting economic diversification, government efficiency, and digital economy development in a large island state with growing connectivity infrastructure and youth demographic.$$,
