      $$São Tomé and Príncipe offers extraordinary tourism potential including pristine tropical beaches, volcanic peaks, endemic biodiversity, Portuguese colonial architecture, plantation heritage, and authentic island culture. Tourism is developing as economic priority. Limited air connectivity and basic hospitality infrastructure constrain growth. Portuguese language and Lisbon connectivity support tourism from Portugal. Eco-tourism and sustainable tourism are development priorities. The sector represents opportunity for beach tourism expansion, eco-tourism development, cultural heritage tourism, diving tourism, and boutique hospitality investment leveraging natural beauty, biodiversity, authenticity, Portuguese heritage, and positioning as unspoiled Gulf of Guinea island paradise serving European and regional tourism markets.$$,
